  "id": "Compound::DB00652 - Gene::4985",
  "verbalization": "Pentazocine is shown to interact with opioid receptors through a shared mechanism of action, as it binds to multiple opioid receptor subtypes—Oprk1, Oprm1, and Sigmar1—each of which participates in opioid receptor activity. This suggests that Pentazocine may exert its effects by modulating the activity of opioid receptors, which are central to the pharmacological profile of opioid analgesics. The evidence indicates that Pentazocine may act on the Oprd1 receptor, as all three receptor subtypes are involved in the same biological process. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Pentazocine influences opioid-related functions, though the exact role of each receptor subtype in the overall effect remains to be fully elucidated. The strong correlation in scores across the three paths supports a consistent relationship between Pentazocine and Oprd1, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
